Usage: python -m fsed.fsed [OPTIONS] PATTERN_FILE [INPUT_FILES]

  Search and replace on INPUT_FILE(s) (or standard input), with matching on
  fixed strings.

Options:
  --pattern-format [auto|tsv|sed]
                                  Specify the format of PATTERN_FILE
                                  [default: auto]
  -o, --output PATH               Program output is written to this file.
                                  Default is to write to standard output.
  -e, --encoding TEXT             The character encoding to use  [default:
                                  utf-8]
  -w, --words                     Match only on word boundaries: appends "\b"
                                  to the beginning and end of every pattern in
                                  PATTERN_FILE.
  --by-line / --across-lines      Process the input line by line or character
                                  by character; the default is --across-lines.
  --slow                          Try very hard to find the longest matches on
                                  the input; this is very slow, and forces
                                  --by-line.
  -v, --verbose                   Turns on debugging output.
  -q, --quiet                     Quiet operation, do not emit warnings.
  --help                          Show this message and exit.
